{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You shall make tassels for yourself.</b> The challengers say it is a commandment unto itself at night, like tzitzit by day; therefore it is written \"which you cover yourself with.\" And the translators translated [it] as though this is the commandment of tzitzit by day, and the meaning of גדלים is like גדלים מעשה שרשרות (tassels of chain-work) in its construction. And the challengers derived it from the root גדול. But we believe in the words of our ancients alone. And this verse was mentioned to explain \"on four corners,\" and it is juxtaposed to sha'atnez because of tzitzit, which is permitted."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Reading המעתיקי' as 'translators'; the referent of the verse citation 'which you cover yourself with' is Deut. 22:12 itself. The phrase 'in its construction' (בבנינה) likely alludes to 1 Kings 7:17; the word העתיקו could mean 'translated' or 'transferred,' resolved as 'translated' given the context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:24.042767828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}